🚀 Day 19 of My Software Engineering Transformation Journey

Hello, this is Sumanth. Today marks Day 19 of my journey toward becoming a Software Engineer.

📅 Date: 30-05-2026
📍 Day: Saturday

Today was all about creating something that I wish I had when I started my DSA preparation.

Instead of solving random problems, I spent time organizing and analyzing interview-focused questions to build a structured roadmap.

📚 What I worked on today:

✅ Organized 337 curated DSA problems
✅ Categorized questions by difficulty
✅ Added company and frequency information
✅ Created a priority-based solving order
✅ Structured the sheet for interview preparation
✅ Reviewed patterns commonly asked in coding interviews

💡 Key realization:

Many students struggle with DSA not because they lack dedication, but because they lack a clear roadmap.

Having the right set of problems and solving them consistently is far more effective than solving hundreds of random questions.

🎯 Current Focus:
• Data Structures & Algorithms
• Problem Solving
• Software Engineering Interview Preparation
• Building Consistency Every Day

Every small improvement compounds over time.

Day 19 complete. On to Day 20. 🚀

